From 8dc7366937c460842133d61c86e08496036033f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Singh <nathan.singh@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 06:56:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Native: the window layer is 64 tiles wide; desktop-only crash
 fixes

The windows' tilemap (menus, messages, the battle HUD) was a 32-tile BG
map, so at 288 pixels its boxes wrapped to the left edge and the battle
command row wrote past it and crashed. Natively it is 64 tiles wide:
WINDOW_MAP_WIDTH and WINDOW_MAP_ROW_SHIFT (window.h; BG_SCREEN_WIDTH and 5
on the GBA) replace the 32 in the window code, WINDOW_TILEMAP_VRAM is a
native wide map and BG0 reads it (BGCNT_NATIVE_WIDE, set where the debug
text screen points BG0 at screen block 4). Three text routines had the
row as "<< 5"; missing them left the HUD without its HP row.

Desktop-only crashes the cartridge shrugs off, at any width:
- The shops' hidden anchor window at x = -5 made the window code read and
  write past the tilemap: Window_DrawBorder, Window_EraseBorderRect and
  Window_ClearTextTilesInRect skip a window off the left edge natively.
- The arena's shops place their cursor before it has a sprite:
  MenuCursor_SetPositionImmediate skips the null anchor natively.

The GBA ROM is byte-identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014ta8ykfbWFo924wEqysLhg
